hts the way...\nIf shadowed thoughts begin to guide the hand,\nThe suffering blooms across the land.\n\n[Chorus]\nMind, mind, chief architect of all we see,\nMind-made reality, wild and free.\nWhen tainted thought takes hold within the core,\nDukkha follows knocking at the door.\nLike the turning wheel beneath the ox's might,\nA heavy burden in the endless light.\n\n[Bridge]\nThe lotus rises from the murky deep,\nWhere seeds of longing endlessly do creep.\nUnstained by mire, yet nourished by the flood,\nReflecting purity within the mud.\nLet us purify this central source we own,\nAnd watch the suffering gently overthrown.\n\n[Guitar Solo/Instrumental Break - evocative, flowing]\n\n[Final Chorus]\nMind, mind, chief architect of all we see,\nMind-made reality, wild and free.\nWhen tainted thought takes hold within the core,\nDukkha follows knocking at the door.\nLike the turning wheel beneath the ox's might,\nA heavy burden in the endless light.\nOh, Mind, let peace begin its steady flight!","suno_style":"Ethereal Indie Folk / Cinematic Ballad. Featuring prominent fingerpicked acoustic guitar, sweeping string pads (simulating a lotus bloom), subtle Tibetan singing bowls, and gentle male vocals with high emotional resonance. Moderate tempo (around 90 BPM). Production should feel vast, contemplative, and deeply peaceful, building intensity towards the final chorus.","word_count":356,"mode":"initial","created_at":"2026-09-07T08:17:09.099Z"},"versions":[{"version":1,"path":"/data/productions/run_1788769016707_917zi2-lyrics-v001.txt","title":"The Wheel of Mind","lyrics":"[Verse 1]\nBefore the sight, before the sound,\nBefore the touch on solid ground,\nThe mind resides, the source untold,\nWhere every story can unfold.\nIt dictates what we see and hear,\nDispelling shadows, calming fear;\nMind precedes all that we claim to know,\nThe seeds of being start to grow.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nBut oh, if this great engine starts to fray,\nA corrupted current lights the way...\nIf shadow